        "title": "Braudel and the Longue Durée",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Fernand Braudel's \"longue durée\" (long duration) is the most influential concept in 20th-century\nFrench historiography. The idea: history operates at multiple temporal scales simultaneously —\nfrom the very slow geological and climatic rhythms that barely move in human time, through\nmedium-term economic and social cycles, to the fast-moving events of conventional history."
    }
